meta {
  name: List Courses
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/courses?page=1&limit=20
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 20
  search:
}

docs {
  Returns a paginated list of all standard/possible courses (e.g. "B.Tech
  Computer Science Engineering", "MBBS", "BBA", "B.Com", "MBA", ...) — a
  deduplicated reference taxonomy, not a college's actual offered courses
  (that's GET /public/colleges/by-slug/:slug/courses). No authentication
  required.

  Query params:
  - search (optional): filter by name (case-insensitive substring match)
  - page (default: 1)
  - limit (default: 20, max: 100)

  Response `data[]` item:
  {
    "id": "CRM-1",
    "name": "Bachelor of Computer Applications (BCA)",
    "slug": "bachelor-of-computer-applications-bca",
    "studyLevel": { "id": "SVL-1", "name": "Undergraduate", "slug": "undergraduate" } | null,
    "stream": { "id": "STR-1", "name": "Computer Science", "slug": "computer-science" },
    "discipline": { "id": "DSC-1", "name": "Computer Applications", "slug": "computer-applications" },
    "programType": { "id": "PGT-1", "name": "Full-time", "slug": "full-time" } | null
  }
  `studyLevel`/`programType` are nullable — a course only requires a
  Discipline (which carries `stream`) at creation time; Study Level and
  Program Type are optional classification fields set separately.
  Meta: { total, page, limit, totalPages }

  Data source: the CourseMaster table (managed via Super Admin →
  Academic Masters → Courses tab, backed by
  /api/v1/admin/universities/courses). Every row is a distinct
  (discipline, study level, program type, name) combination, so this
  list can never contain duplicates. No longer backed by a static JSON
  file — courses.json has been removed.
}
